rusty-av1-toolkit — provenance and third-party notices
======================================================

This repository combines two independent, forked projects, each kept in its
own subdirectory with its full commit history and its own upstream license
files. Nothing in those upstream license files is removed or altered; the
top-level LICENSE is an umbrella that points here.

rusty_av1e/  — AV1 ENCODER
    Fork of rav1e (https://github.com/xiph/rav1e), the AV1 encoder by the
    Alliance for Open Media / rav1e contributors.
    License: BSD 2-Clause  ->  rusty_av1e/LICENSE
    Patents: Alliance for Open Media Patent License 1.0  ->  rusty_av1e/PATENTS
    The AOM patent grant in rusty_av1e/PATENTS travels with the encoder and
    must be retained in any redistribution.

rusty_av1d/  — AV1 DECODER
    Fork of rav1d (https://github.com/memorysafety/rav1d), the safe-Rust port
    of dav1d by VideoLAN / the dav1d authors / Internet Security Research Group.
    License: BSD 2-Clause  ->  rusty_av1d/COPYING

Local modifications
-------------------
The encoder and decoder in this repository are modified from their upstreams
(branches `opt-entropy` and `opt-coeffs` respectively). See each subdirectory's
README/CHANGELOG and the git history for the specific changes.

Both upstreams are BSD 2-Clause licensed; the combined work is distributed
under the same terms (see LICENSE), with the additional AOM patent grant
applying to the rusty_av1e subtree.
